      "writtenOn": "2020-03-19T18:23:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you might be the first person to use an F-string in the project 😊\n\nAll of our style guides predate this feature so none of them mention it. The guides do say to use .format() or the `%` operator, but I think that\u0027s meant as advising against mashing together complicated strings with `+`.\n\nI don\u0027t have an opinion on using f-strings but I expect other people will.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 87,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "a7adbf1b9a3606204e36281f1bff428290e91886",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
